OpenFOAM Workbench (dsh-openfoam-workbench)

This product includes software and ideas derived from the following projects.

1. NullFlux / CFDriver (https://github.com/LZF1111/nullflux)
   Copyright (c) LZF. Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
   The experience-card format (title, domain, triggers, solver, physics, recipe,
   key_params, verify_seq, pitfalls) and the general "inspect -> plan -> run ->
   verify" workflow were adapted from this project. No source files were
   copied: the code, architecture and tool descriptions are original to this
   plugin.

2. dsh-openfoam-doctor (https://github.com/bushizhanghan/dsh-openfoam-doctor)
   Copyright (c) bushizhanghan. Licensed under the MIT License.
   The OpenFOAM dictionary parser, the 31 silent-failure check rules in
   lib/of-engine.js (7 controlDict, 7 fvSchemes, 5 fvSolution, 3 blockMeshDict,
   1 stray times, 4 boundary fields, 4 physics), and the checkMesh/run-log
   parsers, together with the ported test suite and the checkMesh log fixture,
   are derived from this project.
   See licenses/dsh-openfoam-doctor-MIT.txt.

3. csml-rpi/AI-CFD-Scientist (https://github.com/csml-rpi/AI-CFD-Scientist)
   The mesh-independence protocol (STEPS A–E), the numerical-stats patterns,
   the run-validity policy, and the PROCEED/REVISE/RERUN decision taxonomy
   were adapted into our skills. Verify that repository's license before
   redistributing the adapted protocols.

OpenFOAM itself is NOT redistributed. This plugin calls the user's installed
OpenFOAM (GPL-3.0) via subprocesses.
